    "measure_1": {
      "scpi": ":MEASure:ITEM? VPP,CHANnel1;:MEASure:ITEM? VRMS,CHANnel1;:MEASure:ITEM? FREQuency,CHANnel1",
      "scpiFast": ":MEAS:ITEM? VPP,CHAN1;:MEAS:ITEM? VRMS,CHAN1;:MEAS:ITEM? FREQ,CHAN1",
      "description": "Channel 1: Vpp, Vrms and frequency in one round trip.",
      "subsystem": "MEASure",
      "returns": {
        "count": 3,
        "separator": ";",
        "fields": [
          {
            "name": "vpp",
            "type": "NR3",
            "unit": "V"
          },
          {
            "name": "vrms",
            "type": "NR3",
            "unit": "V"
          },
          {
            "name": "freq",
            "type": "NR3",
            "unit": "Hz"
          }
        ]
      },
      "notes": "Rigol takes the source as an ARGUMENT to :MEASure:ITEM?, so these three need no :MEASure:SOURce write and cannot be attributed to the wrong channel. No dB item exists on this firmware — the panel derives dBV from vrms. Authored 2026-08-08 for the tabbed oscilloscope panel; not yet executed against hardware.",
      "unverified": true
    },
    "Get_Stats_CH1": {
      "scpi": ":MEASure:ITEM? VPP,CHANnel1;:MEASure:ITEM? VRMS,CHANnel1;:MEASure:ITEM? FREQuency,CHANnel1;:MEASure:ITEM? PDUTy,CHANnel1",
      "scpiFast": ":MEAS:ITEM? VPP,CHANnel1;:MEAS:ITEM? VRMS,CHANnel1;:MEAS:ITEM? FREQuency,CHANnel1;:MEAS:ITEM? PDUTy,CHANnel1",
      "description": "Get Stats CH1",
      "returns": {
        "count": 4,
        "separator": ";",
        "fields": [
          {
            "name": "vpp_1",
            "type": "NR3",
            "unit": "V"
          },
          {
            "name": "vrms_1",
            "type": "NR3",
            "unit": "V"
          },
          {
            "name": "frequency_1"
          },
          {
            "name": "pduty_1",
            "type": "NR3",
            "unit": "%"
          }
        ]
      },
      "group": "Channel 1 Stats",
      "subsystem": "Channel_1",
      "notes": "Was `:MEASure:VPP? CHANnel1;:MEASure:VRMS? CHANnel1;:MEASure:FREQuency? CHANnel1;:MEASure:PDUTy? CHANnel1`: `:MEASure:VPP?` and its kin are the older DS1000E syntax; the DS1000Z asks every measurement through `:MEASure:ITEM? <item>[,<src>]` (MSO1000Z/DS1000Z Programming Guide p. 2-125, items VPP, VRMS, FREQuency, PDUTy). Same four answers, same order."
    },
